# Normalize text in the repository rather than relying on each contributor's
# core.autocrlf. Without this the behaviour of a clone depends on a global
# git setting, which is how a projection and its .pbl can drift in line
# endings while `git status` stays clean — see
# docs/pb-source-format/encoding.md.
* text=auto eol=lf

# PowerBuilder artefacts must never be normalized: the .pbl stores source
# bytes as given, so a line-ending conversion on the way in or out of git
# silently changes what the compiler sees. No .sr* files live here today;
# this is here so that the first one to arrive is safe.
#
# `-text`, not `binary`, on the sources. Both stop the translation, but
# `binary` is a macro for `-diff -merge -text`, so git would answer
# "Binary files differ" and a PowerBuilder change could not be read in a diff
# — which is exactly what the skills in this repository tell people to avoid.
# The libraries themselves are genuinely opaque, so they stay `binary`.
*.sr* -text
*.pbl binary
*.pbd binary

# Scraped HTML cache and the generated FTS index.
*.db binary
*.sqlite binary
*.sqlite3 binary
